[MATH] the card banner rendered height = 150 CSS pixels, within a 2 pixel tolerance {OBSERVED}
[MATH] the modal banner rendered height = 170 CSS pixels, within a 2 pixel tolerance {OBSERVED}
[DOM] the banner region is visible at a stable reserved height, so the grid does not reflow as banner images load {BL}

[DOM] record which mobile presentation is visible: a swipeable carousel with position dots and a current-of-total indicator as the design specifies, or the paginated single-column grid the implementation ships — a mismatch is DRIFT, reported, never filed {OBSERVED}
[DOM] record whether a mission count is visible in the card footer region as the design specifies, or a pager is present in its place — again DRIFT, reported, never filed {OBSERVED}
[STATE] whichever presentation ships, every mission remains reachable at mobile width and none is stranded behind an unusable control {BL}
[MATH] the content width = the viewport width or less, so no horizontal scrollbar is present {BL}

[MATH] for every interactive control on the page, width >= 24 CSS pixels and height >= 24 CSS pixels — except a control whose measured size = the shipped UI-kit standard for its control type, which is a design-system question and is reported separately {BL}
[MATH] the gap between each pair of adjacent interactive controls >= 8 CSS pixels {BL}
[MATH] for the modal's stepper increment and decrement controls, width >= 24 CSS pixels, height >= 24 CSS pixels and mutual gap >= 8 CSS pixels, since they are the most repeatedly tapped controls in the feature {BL}
[DOM] no control is clipped or pushed outside the viewport at 375 pixels, and every control remains visible {BL}

[MATH] the cumulative layout shift for the page load = 0.1 or less {BL}
[DOM] the balance banner is visible at its reserved height before its value resolves, so the card grid does not jump downward when the balance arrives {BL}
[DOM] each card's banner region is visible at its reserved height before its image loads {BL}
[DOM] the pager is already present in the layout when the grid paints, so it does not appear later and push content downward {BL}

[FORMAT] the two modals render TWO DIFFERENT currency symbols against the same numeric target, so the goal currency travels with the mission {BL}
[MATH] the currency rendered for @td(MSN_ORDERVALUE.name) = @td(MSN_ORDERVALUE.goal_currency), the currency stored on that mission's goal {BL}
[MATH] the currency rendered for @td(MSN_ORDERVALUE_ALTCURRENCY.name) = @td(MSN_ORDERVALUE_ALTCURRENCY.goal_currency) {BL}
[FORMAT] neither modal substitutes the session currency symbol for the goal's own currency {BL}
[MATH] the target number in the first modal = the target number in the second modal, so only the currency differs and any divergence in the number is itself a defect {SPEC}

[DOM] the target block is visible and states the goal, with the literals 'NaN', 'Infinity' and 'undefined' all absent {BL}
[MATH] the modal percent = 0, matching the card, even though the reported current value is above the target {OBSERVED}
[DOM] the modal progress bar fill is visible inside its track and does not overflow it {BL}
[MATH] the modal reward line = @td(MSN_ZEROTARGET.reward), the zero-TARGET fixture's own reward, and not the zero-REWARD fixture's {OBSERVED}
[DOM] a Close control is present and the modal can be dismissed {OBSERVED}

[DOM] a live region or an alert role is present on the error surface, so its arrival is announced to assistive technology rather than only painted {BL}
[DOM] the 'Try again' control exposes a non-empty accessible name and is reachable by keyboard alone {BL}
[DOM] focus is present on the error surface once it replaces the grid, so a keyboard user is not left focused on a removed element {BL}
[DOM] after recovery the arrival of the mission grid is likewise announced, and a silent swap with no live region present is absent {BL}
[DOM] a live region is likewise present on the no-missions empty state, and its announced text is distinguishable from the failure announcement by wording alone {BL}

[DOM] every card title is visible and non-empty in the untranslated locale {BL}
[DOM] the localized fixture falls back to @td(MSN_LOCALIZED.name_default), and a blank title, the literal 'null' and a dotted translation key are all absent {BL}
[DOM] the modal title and description fall back the same way, and an empty title region or empty description region is absent {BL}
[DOM] the surrounding chrome falls back to the storefront default language, and a raw dotted key is absent from every visible label {BL}
